[00:04.29] Down from the glen came the marching men
[00:09.24] With their shields and their swords
[00:12.84] To fight the fight they believed to be right
[00:17.29] Overthrow the overlords
[00:21.49] To the towns where there was plenty
[00:25.55] They brought plunder, swords and flame
[00:29.24] When they left, the town was empty
[00:33.11] And children would never play again
[00:36.51] 
[00:55.23] From their graves I heard the fallen
[00:59.46] Above the battle cry
[01:03.55] By that bridge near the border
[01:07.55] There were many more to die
[01:11.50] Then onward over the mountain
[01:15.66] And outward towards the sea
[01:19.51] They had come to claim the Emerald
[01:23.79] Without it, they could not leave
[01:26.16] 